    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0222" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/2–846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-09T16:00:00-05:00">February 9, 1946—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>227. For Cabot only. We deeply appreciate and have carefully weighed the
                    considerations set forth in urtel 430, Feb. 8.
                    However, on net balance it has been decided to give statement to press Mon.
                    about 6 p.m. Washington time with 24 hour release date. Summary being cabled in
                        cirtel<anchor n="50" xml:id="d170-f1"/>
                    today.</p>
                <p>Dept feels this is right course action and the one least vulnerable to criticism
                    from points of view of principle and long-range policy and objectives.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
